  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s F17 drawing. Its tile corners were snapped to the square-root-of-two grid in small-star-radius units. The unit-star opening is shared with the other Moroccan reconstructions. After it every line, the tile’s sides too, is drawn through a crossing of earlier lines and turned round O. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The tile edges follow the plain drawing. The colours follow Wichmann’s drawing, which keeps the original colouring, in the Tétouan palette, whose dark navy stands for his black; his blue and light green, which the palette lacks, are fixed colours. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
      "source": "Tiling Search, data166/F17: Royal residence, Telouet",
      "creator": "Brian Wichmann",
      "kind": "drawing",
      "url": "https://tilingsearch.mit.edu/HTML/data166/F17.html",
      "note": "Read from his finished drawing, not construction instructions. His reference is André Paccard, Traditional Islamic Craft in Moroccan Architecture (1980), volume 2, page 315, the royal residence at Telouet (part of a larger pattern, colours from the original)."
    }
